From cc6a6fe26fa13b3095fb2b274b5692285be9760f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Alonso <nick@drkm.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:54:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] Warn when kv_bits cannot apply, CPU exactness test,
 acknowledgment

maybe_quantize_kv_cache stayed silent when no cache of the model supports
quantization (CacheList models such as Inkling); it now warns once. The
Inkling tests gain a CPU-device fp32 check of decode and chunked prefill
against the full forward at 1e-5 (exact matmuls, no TF32) and a test for the
warning; the short-conv docstring states that kernel and compiled taps agree
after rounding to the activation dtype.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
